# Build output
/sqlb
/dist/
*.exe

# Test and coverage artefacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Node, for the example's generated TypeScript client. The lockfile is tracked;
# what it installs is not.
node_modules/

# Dart, for the example's generated client. Same rule: pubspec.lock is tracked,
# the package cache and analyser state it produces are not.
.dart_tool/

# The scratch directory `sqlb` compiles its driver in. It lives inside the
# target module rather than in /tmp, because Go refuses an internal/ import from
# a file outside the module (cmd/sqlb/driver.go says why at length) — so it
# appears in whichever module was generated from, including the examples here.
# The command removes it on the way out and on a signal, and sweeps stale ones
# left by a kill it could not observe; this rule is what keeps the window
# between those from ending in a commit, which has already happened once.
.sqlb-driver-*/

# The scratch directory codegen's compile check generates into. Same shape and
# same reason as the one above: it has to live inside this module, because that
# is what resolves the sqlb and huma imports in the code being compiled. The
# test removes it, and this rule covers the run that is killed before it can.
.sqlb-gencheck-*/

# Local environment
.env
.env.local

# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Session handoff notes. Working scaffolding addressed to the next session, not
# project documentation: they carry local paths, point-in-time commit shas and
# live TODOs. What is durable in them belongs in docs/adr or docs/ instead.
.handoffs/
